   toggle->collapse), asserting after EVERY step that (a) the rendered
   chart's category set/order (trace.y, since renderChart swaps x/y for
   #chart-trends's horizontal-bar orientation, charts.js:181-183) equals
   the table's visible data-category list, (b) height ==
   max(360, n*38+120), (c) trace0.marker.color === current --accent
   (non-array) and trace1.marker.color === current prior hex. Verified
   light/dark accent values genuinely differ (rgb(79,70,229) vs
   rgb(165,180,252); #78716c vs #a8a29e) so the marker check is
   non-vacuous. Result across 2 ranges x 2 orderings x 5 steps = 20
   states: ZERO category-set/order errors, ZERO marker-color errors in
   any state or ordering -- the attempt-1 stale-theme defect
   (TC-2026-09-08b) is fixed for every sequence tried, including the
   adversarial "interact immediately after toggle" and "toggle mid-sort"
   orders the ruling didn't explicitly enumerate.

